WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.052
Possessives and Plurals

00:00:02.432 --> 00:00:05.847
Apostrophes show ownership. Never plurals.

00:00:07.047 --> 00:00:08.046
How to spot it

00:00:08.446 --> 00:00:10.775
The same word, apostrophe moved

00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:13.207
A noun followed by what it might own

00:00:13.757 --> 00:00:16.698
It’s testing: plurals versus possessives

00:00:17.898 --> 00:00:18.693
The method

00:00:19.093 --> 00:00:21.587
Step 1: Does it own the next word?

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:23.688
No? No apostrophe.

00:00:24.238 --> 00:00:26.559
Step 2: One owner or many?

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:28.812
Look for clues like “two” or “its”.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.813
Step 3: Place the apostrophe

00:00:32.093 --> 00:00:36.341
One owner: ’s. Many: s’.

00:00:36.891 --> 00:00:39.578
Step 4: Pronouns never take one

00:00:39.858 --> 00:00:41.357
its, their, whose

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:43.017
In a few words

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:44.894
Own it? One or many?

00:00:46.094 --> 00:00:46.917
The rules

00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:48.882
Plural: just s

00:00:49.162 --> 00:00:51.037
Wrong: The plant’s bloom.

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.082
Right: The plants bloom.

00:00:53.632 --> 00:00:55.881
One owner: ’s

00:00:56.161 --> 00:00:58.027
Right: the singer’s album

00:00:58.577 --> 00:01:00.990
Many owners: s’

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:03.353
Right: the residents’ campaign

00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:06.748
Irregular plurals: ’s

00:01:07.028 --> 00:01:09.060
Wrong: the childrens’ section

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:11.310
Right: the children’s section

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.329
its = possessive, it’s = it is

00:01:14.609 --> 00:01:16.987
Wrong: The town and it’s festival

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:19.553
Right: The town and its festival

00:01:20.103 --> 00:01:22.319
Decades: no apostrophe

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:24.671
Wrong: the 1950’s

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.933
Right: the 1950s

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:29.173
Let’s try one

00:01:29.582 --> 00:01:36.272
In the 1960s, the ______ campaign to protect the wetland convinced the state to declare it a nature

00:01:36.272 --> 00:01:36.926
reserve.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.685
Does the word own the next one?

00:01:39.685 --> 00:01:42.417
The campaign belongs to the residents.

00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:44.387
So yes, it’s possessive.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:50.092
One resident, or many? Residents organising a campaign: many.

00:01:50.642 --> 00:01:54.616
Many owners: s, then the apostrophe. Choice C.

00:01:55.816 --> 00:01:56.812
Common traps

00:01:57.212 --> 00:01:58.662
The plural apostrophe

00:01:58.942 --> 00:02:01.817
If nothing is owned, there’s no apostrophe.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.472
it’s vs its

00:02:03.752 --> 00:02:06.632
Say “it is”. If it breaks, use its.

00:02:07.832 --> 00:02:09.284
Possessives and Plurals

00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:11.292
Own it? One or many?

00:02:11.842 --> 00:02:12.615
Spot it

00:02:12.815 --> 00:02:15.343
Same word, apostrophe moved around

00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:16.600
Steps

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.802
1. Does it own the next word?

00:02:19.082 --> 00:02:20.877
2. One owner or many?

00:02:21.157 --> 00:02:25.537
3. One: ’s · Many: s’

00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:29.169
4. Pronouns never: its, their, whose

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:30.471
Remember

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.695
Plural = just s (the plants)

00:02:32.975 --> 00:02:36.770
children’s, women’s (irregular + ’s)

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.135
its = belongs to it; it’s = it is

00:02:40.415 --> 00:02:42.744
1950s (no apostrophe)

00:02:43.294 --> 00:02:43.899
Trap

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:46.120
An apostrophe on a plain plural

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.565
